    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc01fe8a_5e2a876d",
        "filename": "gm/surface_factory/RasterSurfaceFactory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T20:53:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current behavior in BazelGMRunner.cpp is to print a warning and skip the GM if the surface couldn\u0027t be created. I changed that logic to make the entire Bazel test fail instead of just skipping the GM. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "2a73ce44_dfdb1323",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "49946517f0a9a4418733837f7966d3cd4c2562b4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98662a9a_463b3763",
        "filename": "gm/surface_factory/RasterSurfaceFactory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T21:34:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also updated the follow-up CL (https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/721915) to use `SkASSERT_RELEASE` in the factories if the surface/context couldn\u0027t be created for reasons other than an unknown config.\n\nI think this is a good balance: we fail early if something goes wrong during surface creation time, and we print a meaningful error message if the config passed to BazelGMRunner.cpp via the `--config` flag is unknown (not to be confused with Bazel\u0027s own `--config` flag).",
      "parentUuid": "bc01fe8a_5e2a876d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "49946517f0a9a4418733837f7966d3cd4c2562b4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "787e37a1_ff04e659",
        "filename": "gm/surface_factory/RasterSurfaceFactory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-13T15:08:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should always assert/abort (the equivalent of panic) if we cannot set up a surface. Using failures should be reserved for \"we had problems while drawing\" not \"we had problems before drawing\".\n\nYou got me thinking, \"config\" is a bit overloaded. As long as we are re-creating things, can we call it --surface_config to differentiate it from the bazel flag and give it slightly more meaning?",
      "parentUuid": "98662a9a_463b3763",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "49946517f0a9a4418733837f7966d3cd4c2562b4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1afe4de_37397d08",
        "filename": "gm/surface_factory/RasterSurfaceFactory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-13T19:57:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, aborting if we had problems before drawing makes sense to me.\n\nIn order to avoid repeating the same `SK_ABORT` message on all factories, I placed the `SK_ABORT` in BazelGMRunner.cpp when the returned surface is nil, and I updated the comment in SurfaceFactory.h to explicitly state the contract that `make_surface` must only return null if the config is unknown, and abort execution on all other errors.",
      "parentUuid": "787e37a1_ff04e659",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "49946517f0a9a4418733837f7966d3cd4c2562b4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
